e 14 only concerns local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 applies only to elected officials"'::jsonb, '"Always disregard Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recognizing enforceable rights and the directive role of Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as criminal offences"'::jsonb, '"Assume both Parts have identical justiciability"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400912101010110, ARRAY['"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A law makes an unequal classification. The government explains a legitimate aim, but the classification has no rational connection to that aim. Which issue remains?"'::jsonb, '"A person is denied personal liberty under an executive order with no lawful procedure. The authority says that administrative convenience is sufficient. Which response best reflects Article 21?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as abolishing the essential democratic character of the Constitution. Which sequence of analysis is most appropriate for a course-level answer?"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble''s words ''Secular'' and ''Socialist'' were inserted by an amendment. Which statement about that history is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Duty to protect the environment is cited to automatically deny a person''s otherwise lawful speech. Which conclusion is most careful?"'::jsonb, '"A new state policy is consistent with a Directive Principle but is implemented in a way that violates Article 21. What follows?"'::jsonb, '"A state Governor and a Chief Minister disagree about the ordinary political direction of a state government. Which principle best describes their normal roles?"'::jsonb, '"A city and a rural district are designing local institutions. Which pairing is most consistent with the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A student says the ECI is responsible for every municipal poll because Article 324 covers elections. What is the best correction?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Whether it was published in a newspaper"'::jsonb, '"Whether the Governor attended a meeting"'::jsonb, '"Whether a municipal ward has been renumbered"'::jsonb, '"Whether the classification meets Article 14''s equality/non-arbitrariness requirements"'::jsonb, '"Personal liberty cannot be deprived except according to procedure established by law"'::jsonb, '"Convenience always overrides liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to corporations"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 concerns only the right to vote"'::jsonb, '"Check only whether the amendment title contains the word democratic"'::jsonb, '"Identify the alleged basic feature and assess it under the basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Ask the municipal corporation to ratify the amendment"'::jsonb, '"Treat every amendment as automatically invalid"'::jsonb, '"They were included only by the 86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"They were added to the original text in 1947"'::jsonb, '"They were added by the 42nd Amendment in 1976"'::jsonb, '"They are found only in Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties automatically override every right"'::jsonb, '"Environmental protection is not mentioned in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A applies only to municipal officers"'::jsonb, '"The duty is relevant, but a restriction on speech must still be assessed under the constitutional provisions governing that freedom"'::jsonb, '"Its policy objective alone does not eliminate the need to comply with applicable Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Part IV automatically overrides Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 does not apply to government action"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament''s Speaker can evaluate it"'::jsonb, '"The Governor is the elected day-to-day political leader"'::jsonb, '"The Governor is constitutional head while the Chief Minister leads the elected government and Council of Ministers"'::jsonb, '"The Chief Minister is appointed by the municipal corporation"'::jsonb, '"The District Collector is the constitutional head of the state"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation—rural district; Zila Panchayat—Union legislature"'::jsonb, '"Both bodies are election courts"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation—urban local government; Zila Panchayat—district-level rural local government"'::jsonb, '"Zila Panchayat—House of Parliament; Municipal Corporation—state Cabinet"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 covers only school elections"'::jsonb, '"Municipal polls are run by Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"No constitutional body administers local elections"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution separately provides State Election Commissions for Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400912101010111, ARRAY['"A law classifies citizens by a criterion unrelated to its stated goal; affected people also claim the criterion burdens an Article 19 freedom. What is the strongest analytical approach?"'::jsonb, '"An administrator relies on an environmental duty to justify all restrictions on a public meeting. What should a balanced legal analysis do?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional amendment changes the composition of a body, and challengers claim the change damages separation of powers and judicial review. What evidence is most important to the basic-structure question?"'::jsonb, '"A welfare scheme relies on a Directive Principle and denies a benefit through an arbitrary process. What is the most accurate conclusion?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen challenges an order affecting personal liberty. The authority claims Article 21 only applies when a law is completely absent, not when procedure exists but is arbitrary. Which response best reflects modern constitutional reasoning at course level?"'::jsonb, '"An interpretation dispute involves an ambiguous provision. One interpretation better advances justice, liberty and equality while remaining consistent with the text. How may the Preamble be used?"'::jsonb, '"The Union government loses Lok Sabha confidence but claims the Council of Ministers answers only to Rajya Sabha. Which constitutional feature refutes the claim?"'::jsonb, '"An election dispute concerns a Lok Sabha constituency, while a separate dispute concerns a municipal ward poll. Which institutional distinction is relevant at the outset?"'::jsonb, '"A person says all Directive Principles are individually enforceable in court because they are ''fundamental in governance''. Which reasoning corrects the conflation?"'::jsonb, '"A government claims equal protection demands the same outcome for every person regardless of materially relevant differences. What response is more accurate?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Assess equality/non-arbitrariness under Article 14 and separately test any Article 19 restriction against its applicable constitutional grounds"'::jsonb, '"Assume a single Article automatically decides all claims"'::jsonb, '"Treat the matter only as a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Refer the policy to a Zila Panchayat for constitutional interpretation"'::jsonb, '"Reject environmental protection as a constitutional concern"'::jsonb, '"Recognize Article 51A''s environmental duty but independently assess the restriction under the applicable rights and lawful procedure"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 51A as the only enforceable right"'::jsonb, '"Assume public meetings are always prohibited"'::jsonb, '"Whether a state Governor publicly supports the amendment"'::jsonb, '"How many local wards exist"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s actual legal effects on the alleged foundational features, considered under the basic-structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Whether the amendment uses formal language"'::jsonb, '"Because welfare is a goal, all procedures are valid"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles are meaningless and must be ignored"'::jsonb, '"The denial can never be reviewed"'::jsonb, '"The scheme''s objective may be relevant, but its arbitrary implementation can still raise Article 14 concerns"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection includes scrutiny of the legal procedure affecting life and liberty; the existence of a procedure alone does not end analysis"'::jsonb, '"Any written procedure automatically validates every deprivation"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 only applies during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 and 21 cannot ever be considered together"'::jsonb, '"As an authority to disregard the operative text"'::jsonb, '"As an interpretive aid that illuminates constitutional objectives while the provision''s text remains controlling"'::jsonb, '"As a substitute for all judicial reasoning"'::jsonb, '"As a local administration manual"'::jsonb, '"The President presides over Rajya Sabha daily"'::jsonb, '"State Governors supervise Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Collective responsibility to Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"The State Election Commission''s municipal remit"'::jsonb, '"Both are necessarily conducted by Municipal Corporation itself"'::jsonb, '"Both are conducted only by the Supreme Court"'::jsonb, '"The President organizes both directly"'::jsonb, '"ECI administers the parliamentary election; State EC administers municipal elections under the local-body framework"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 expressly distinguishes their governance importance from direct court enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is actually Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A makes every policy court-enforceable"'::jsonb, '"Only the President can decide enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 prohibits all different treatment"'::jsonb, '"Equal protection allows reasonable classification but not arbitrary discrimination"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only applies to local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 overrides every other provision automatically"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400912101010112, ARRAY['"A law limits a citizen''s expression, uses a classification that may be arbitrary, and is defended as advancing a public-policy objective. Which review sequence is most defensible?"'::jsonb, '"A parent fails to provide educational opportunities to a child aged 8. Which pair most accurately separates a Fundamental Duty from the related right?"'::jsonb, '"A local administration proposal mixes city drainage services and district rural development. Which institutional design best reflects the course distinctions?"'::jsonb, '"A student must explain why constitutionalism matters when officials exercise emergency-like discretion. Which answer is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as undermining a foundational feature, but the challenger merely says the new text is different. What must the argument add?"'::jsonb, '"A student states the Election Commission of India administers municipal elections because Article 324 concerns election control. Which constitutional arrangement resolves the point?"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A person cites a Directive Principle as the sole basis to demand a directly enforceable order. Which qualification should be included?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional issue concerns equal treatment, personal liberty and a policy directive. Which response is methodologically sound?"'::jsonb, '"A local government officer claims their administrative decisions are outside constitutional limits because the office is local, not national. Which principle best answers that claim?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Accept the objective as conclusive and stop"'::jsonb, '"Review only the Preamble, ignoring the Articles"'::jsonb, '"Examine the relevant Article 19 ground/reasonableness, assess the classification under Article 14, and consider the policy objective without treating it as a complete defence"'::jsonb, '"Apply Article 324 because every public dispute is electoral"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 is the duty and Article 19 is the right"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 is the duty and Article 51A is a right"'::jsonb, '"The 73rd Amendment creates both"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k) states the parental/guardian duty; Article 21A concerns the right to education for ages 6–14"'::jsonb, '"Use the Municipal Corporation for urban local-government functions and the Zila Panchayat for district-level rural local government, subject to applicable state arrangements"'::jsonb, '"Give both tasks to the Rajya Sabha"'::jsonb, '"Assign both to the Election Commission of India"'::jsonb, '"Treat both as functions of the Prime Minister personally"'::jsonb, '"It means officials may ignore law if their goal seems useful"'::jsonb, '"It means power is structured and limited by constitutional rules, rights and institutional checks"'::jsonb, '"It means there is no separation of functions"'::jsonb, '"It means only local bodies are bound by laws"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s page count"'::jsonb, '"The names of all members of the legislature"'::jsonb, '"A reasoned connection between the amendment''s practical/legal effect and an alleged basic feature"'::jsonb, '"Only the date it was introduced"'::jsonb, '"Municipal elections are outside the Constitution entirely"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation appoints ECI members"'::jsonb, '"Lok Sabha runs municipal wards directly"'::jsonb, '"Part IXA provides a State Election Commission framework for municipality elections, while ECI handles elections assigned under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Recognize the environmental aim and Article 51A duty, while also assessing whether the decision complies with applicable rights such as Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Treat the environmental aim as an automatic exemption from equality"'::jsonb, '"Assume Article 14 applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Assume Fundamental Duties erase all legal procedures"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles are superior to every constitutional right"'::jsonb, '"They guide State policy and are important in governance, but Article 37 says they are not directly enforceable by courts"'::jsonb, '"They apply only to local councils"'::jsonb, '"They are listed in Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Apply only Article 51A to every dispute"'::jsonb, '"Assume Part IV repeals Part III"'::jsonb, '"Identify the separate questions under Article 14, Article 21 and Part IV, then interpret them together rather than treating one as automatic trump"'::jsonb, '"Refer it to a municipal corporation as the final constitutional court"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament must follow law"'::jsonb, '"Constitutionalism applies only during general elections"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights apply only to Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Public authorities at all levels must act within applicable constitutional and legal limits"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);
COMMIT;
